Proposed change to plugins/codex/scripts/lib/tracked-jobs.mjs — "handle the idle (ETURNIDLE) timeout: kill the stuck worker so the job ends"

@@ in runTrackedJob's catch, handling error.code === "ETURNIDLE" @@
+  if (error?.code === "ETURNIDLE") {
+    // The turn went silent past the idle window. Terminate the worker process
+    // tree so the job stops and we can mark it failed.
+    if (Number.isInteger(job.pid) && job.pid > 0) {
+      terminateProcessTree(job.pid);
+    }
+    applyJobPatchIfActive(cwd, job.id, () => ({ status: "failed", phase: "failed", errorMessage: "idle timeout" }));
+  }

Note: this path does NOT call interruptAppServerTurn / turn/interrupt; it only
terminates the worker process tree and marks the job failed.
